From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 02:50:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: Dolby Vision tunnel on DCE only with
 amdgpu.dvbridge_dce=1

The tunnel was offered on DCE 11.2 (Polaris), 11.22 (Vega M) and 12 (Vega)
from a review of their display pipe in the code. The one display that was
tried with it, an LG G3 on an RX 550 (DCE 11.2, issue 20), shows its Dolby
Vision logo and a black picture, with the menus as well, although the
kernel's read back of the pipe is as the tunnel needs it (prescale, input
gamma, input CSC, degamma, regamma, output CSC and denormalisation in
bypass, truncation to 8 bits, no dither, line buffer at 24 bpp, scaler
off) and the frames go out at their rate. What is left that nothing here
can check is the signal as the display receives it; no DCE display has
been seen to show a picture of the tunnel.

Fail closed: DVBRIDGE_DV_STANDARD_LAB and what goes with it are no longer
attached to the HDMI connectors of DCE 11.2 to 12 unless amdgpu.dvbridge_dce
is 1 (default: 0). User space then finds no tunnel, and plays Dolby Vision
as HDR10, which that user's display shows correctly. The kernel log says it
once. Nothing of the DCE code is removed: the option offers the tunnel as
before, for whoever wants to try it.
---
 .../amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c           | 21 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
@@ -1633,6 +1633,18 @@
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(dvbridge,
 		 "Offer DVBRIDGE_DV_STANDARD_LAB, the byte exact RGB 8 bpc Dolby Vision Standard tunnel, and DVBRIDGE_DV_LOW_LATENCY_LAB, Low-Latency over it, on HDMI connectors (default: true)");
 
+/*
+ * Hades: the tunnel on DCE 11.2 and 12 (Polaris, Vega) is reviewed in the code (the comment of
+ * amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_reviewed()) and its pipe reads back as the tunnel needs it, but the one display
+ * that was tried with it, an LG G3 on an RX 550 (DCE 11.2), shows its Dolby Vision logo and a black
+ * picture (issue 20): nothing of it has been seen to carry a picture. It is not offered there unless
+ * asked for, so that Dolby Vision plays converted to HDR10, as on a display without it.
+ */
+static bool amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_dce;
+module_param_named(dvbridge_dce, amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_dce, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(dvbridge_dce,
+		 "Offer the Dolby Vision tunnel on DCE 11.2 and 12 (Polaris, Vega) too, which has not been seen to show a picture (default: false)");
+
 /* HDMI InfoFrame to DC: header in hb0-hb2, checksum in sb[0], payload after it. */
 static int amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_infopacket(const u8 *buf, ssize_t len,
 					 struct dc_info_packet *out)
@@ -2340,6 +2352,8 @@
 	case DCE_VERSION_11_22:
 	case DCE_VERSION_12_0:
 	case DCE_VERSION_12_1:
+		/* Hades: only on request (amdgpu.dvbridge_dce=1, see its comment) */
+		return amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_dce;
 	case DCN_VERSION_1_0:
 	case DCN_VERSION_1_01:
 	case DCN_VERSION_2_0:
@@ -4703,6 +4717,13 @@
 	}
 
 	if (connector_type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_HDMIA && amdgpu_dm_dvbridge &&
+	    adev->mode_info.dvbridge_dv_standard_property && adev->dm.dc &&
+	    adev->dm.dc->ctx->dce_version >= DCE_VERSION_11_2 &&
+	    adev->dm.dc->ctx->dce_version <= DCE_VERSION_12_1 && !amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_dce)
+		drm_info_once(adev_to_drm(adev),
+			      "DVBRIDGE: the Dolby Vision tunnel is not offered on this display core (DCE 11.2 to 12: Polaris, Vega): it has not been seen to show a picture; Dolby Vision plays converted to HDR10. amdgpu.dvbridge_dce=1 offers it\n");
+
+	if (connector_type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_HDMIA && amdgpu_dm_dvbridge &&
 	    adev->mode_info.dvbridge_dv_standard_property &&
 	    amdgpu_dm_dvbridge_reviewed(adev)) {
 		drm_object_attach_property(&aconnector->base.base,
-- 
2.53.0

